{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787769513,"nonce":"fqRC2DlS15fEyhv1dV+I1dZmyYE=","title":"Collision sample step-ids are remapped at settle, not launch (2e1a458 residual)","message":"Found by the skeptical review of feat/2e1a458-loud-fanin (LOW).\n\nrecord_workspace_collisions (scheduler.rs ~:2310) rebuilds output_of from SETTLE-time step_output, but the fetcher's root indices were minted from LAUNCH-time output_of (~:2006). If an upstream step gains or loses an output between launch and settle (concurrent rerun / new take), the winner/loser step ids in a WorkspaceInputCollisions sample can misattribute. The COUNT stays correct, and the event is best-effort evidence by contract, so this is an accuracy wart rather than a correctness bug.\n\nFix direction: record the launch-time root-\u003estep list (it is already computed to mint WSFETCH_ROOTS) and resolve the sample against that instead of re-deriving at settle.","files":null}]}